1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:01,467
<i> Sorry, that was embarrassing.</i>

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:02,533
<i>You don't have to say sorry,
okay?</i>

3
00:00:02,667 --> 00:00:04,100
<i>You have nothing to do
with this.</i>

4
00:00:04,233 --> 00:00:05,533
<i> It's between me and Andrew.</i>

5
00:00:05,667 --> 00:00:06,967
<i>Yeah, I know.
I have nothing to do</i>

6
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:08,467
<i> with your real relationship.</i>

7
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:09,733
<i> Are you jealous?</i>

8
00:00:09,867 --> 00:00:11,033
<i> Me? Jealous?</i>

9
00:00:11,167 --> 00:00:11,933
<i> No way.</i>

10
00:00:12,067 --> 00:00:13,367
<i> Let's talk about this later.</i>

11
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:14,667
<i> Someone might see us.</i>

12
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:16,500
<i>I'll see you tomorrow, Clarissa.</i>

13
00:00:16,633 --> 00:00:17,700
<i> I like her.</i>

14
00:00:17,833 --> 00:00:19,600
<i>I hope she doesn't give up
easily.</i>

15
00:00:19,733 --> 00:00:20,933
<i> Then be nice to her.</i>

16
00:00:21,067 --> 00:00:22,467
<i> Hey, what are you peeking at?</i>

17
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,067
<i>I'm not planning to steal
anything here.</i>

18
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:25,033
<i> Enough talk!</i>

19
00:00:25,167 --> 00:00:28,000
<i> [GRUNTING AND GROANING]</i>

20
00:00:28,133 --> 00:00:29,200
<i> I said I don't want trouble!</i>

21
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:30,400
<i> What are you doing?</i>

22
00:00:30,533 --> 00:00:31,433
<i> My companion went missing,</i>

23
00:00:31,567 --> 00:00:33,233
<i>so I was going to bring this
to the room.</i>

24
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:34,433
<i> I thought you left me.</i>

25
00:00:34,567 --> 00:00:35,733
<i> I have a question for you.</i>

26
00:00:35,867 --> 00:00:38,133
<i>Madam Delilah,
what do you do for her?</i>

27
00:00:38,267 --> 00:00:40,667
<i>Maybe I can apply for a job
with your boss.</i>

28
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:42,833
<i>Tomorrow, I'll introduce you
to my boss.</i>

29
00:00:42,967 --> 00:00:44,000
<i> That's a promis, okay?</i>

30
00:00:44,133 --> 00:00:46,100
<i>- I'm sorry.
- Why are you apologizing?</i>

31
00:00:46,233 --> 00:00:47,700
<i> You don't have to apologize.</i>

32
00:00:47,833 --> 00:00:50,000
<i>If you two get back together,
then go ahead.</i>

33
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,167
<i>I want something different now.</i>

34
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:52,500
<i> There you are!</i>

35
00:00:52,633 --> 00:00:54,233
<i> How are my two lovebirds?</i>

36
00:00:54,367 --> 00:00:55,733
<i> We'll treat you to dinner.</i>

37
00:00:55,867 --> 00:00:57,200
<i> I have to decline</i>

38
00:00:57,333 --> 00:00:59,967
<i>because I have a very important
meeting tomorrow night.</i>

39
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:03,767
<i>I'm sure Berdugo is the one
Delilah's meeting with.</i>

40
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:05,233
<i>Let's talk about this tomorrow.</i>

41
00:01:05,367 --> 00:01:06,233
<i> There's still time.</i>

42
00:01:06,367 --> 00:01:07,467
<i> I'm really sleepy.</i>

43
00:01:07,633 --> 00:01:09,267
<i>I thought you weren't mad at me
anymore?</i>

44
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:10,533
<i> Why does it hurt?</i>

45
00:01:10,667 --> 00:01:12,000
<i> We're not even together.</i>

46
00:01:12,133 --> 00:01:13,633
<i> I don't want you anymore.</i>

47
00:01:13,767 --> 00:01:15,500
<i> Why am I affected?</i>

48
00:01:15,633 --> 00:01:18,667
<i>Would I be happy
if we get back together?</i>

49
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:21,533
<i>I already know
what will make me happy.</i>

50
00:01:24,033 --> 00:01:26,300
<i> [OBB]</i>

51
00:01:39,733 --> 00:01:40,867
Don't worry, Boss.

52
00:01:41,033 --> 00:01:42,600
I'll take care
of my fellow officers.

53
00:01:42,733 --> 00:01:45,933
I'll make sure your service
to me is rewarded.

54
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:02,033
Oh, Sir...

55
00:02:02,167 --> 00:02:04,333
Ma'am Delilah is expecting you.

56
00:02:04,467 --> 00:02:05,767
Your villa is ready.

57
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:08,767
Boss, just follow my car, okay?

58
00:02:12,867 --> 00:02:16,767
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

59
00:02:16,933 --> 00:02:18,033
So, Boss?

60
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,267
I'll come back tomorrow morning.

61
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,233
Okay.

62
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,700
Make sure nothing goes wrong
tomorrow, okay?

63
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:26,067
Yes, Boss.

64
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:29,000
But Matias mentioned

65
00:02:29,133 --> 00:02:30,633
someone's been asking about you.

66
00:02:30,767 --> 00:02:31,900
Is that true?

67
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:33,833
Who?

68
00:02:35,867 --> 00:02:37,333
Have you met them?

69
00:02:37,467 --> 00:02:39,833
That's the problem, Boss,
I didn't recognize them.

70
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:42,233
But if ever I do recognize them,

71
00:02:42,733 --> 00:02:44,533
I'll definitely know
who they are for sure.

72
00:02:47,767 --> 00:02:49,067
All right, Boss, I'll go ahead.

73
00:02:54,267 --> 00:02:56,833
[CAR REVVING]

74
00:02:56,967 --> 00:02:59,900
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

75
00:03:03,367 --> 00:03:06,033
[MOTORCYCLE REVVING]

76
00:03:11,067 --> 00:03:17,867
[PHONE RINGING]

77
00:03:20,133 --> 00:03:24,400
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:03:26,767 --> 00:03:27,967
<i> Joey?</i>

79
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:29,000
Dad?

80
00:03:29,133 --> 00:03:31,167
Finally, I am able
to see your face, Joey.

81
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:32,967
<i> How are you? I've missed you.</i>

82
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:34,967
Where's your mother?

83
00:03:35,333 --> 00:03:36,600
Did you tell her?

84
00:03:37,233 --> 00:03:38,933
I'll talk to her.

85
00:03:39,633 --> 00:03:41,833
Dad, mom's not here right now.

86
00:03:41,967 --> 00:03:43,167
Where is she?

87
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:45,167
I'm sorry, Dad, but...

88
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,733
I haven't gone home yet.

89
00:03:47,867 --> 00:03:48,967
What?

90
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:50,367
<i> Where are you?</i>

91
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:53,033
Joey?

92
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:56,400
Who is that?
Is that Andrew?

93
00:03:58,867 --> 00:04:00,567
Joey, your father's alive?

94
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:03,733
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

95
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:06,933
This is why I can move
freely now...

96
00:04:07,067 --> 00:04:08,800
because the syndicate thinks

97
00:04:08,933 --> 00:04:10,100
I'm dead.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

98
00:04:10,233 --> 00:04:12,633
<i>Honestly, this might be
the wildest</i>

99
00:04:12,767 --> 00:04:14,767
<i> yet smartest undercover strat</i>

100
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:19,300
<i>I've ever witnessed
in my entire journalism career.</i>

101
00:04:19,433 --> 00:04:20,833
I can't believe this.

102
00:04:21,267 --> 00:04:23,800
Hey, you talk about
my dad's situation

103
00:04:23,933 --> 00:04:25,633
like it's a news article.

104
00:04:25,767 --> 00:04:27,300
It's not like that.

105
00:04:27,467 --> 00:04:29,200
I just can't believe it.

106
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,733
I mean, of course,
I had to understand everything

107
00:04:31,867 --> 00:04:33,367
because I want to help your dad.

108
00:04:34,033 --> 00:04:35,967
That's exactly why we're here,
right?

109
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:37,500
<i> You know, to be honest...</i>

110
00:04:37,633 --> 00:04:39,467
you shouldn't be doing this.

111
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:40,900
<i>You're not supposed to be there.</i>

112
00:04:41,033 --> 00:04:42,067
<i> You should go home.</i>

113
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:44,200
You might get in trouble.
It's dangerous.

114
00:04:44,333 --> 00:04:46,767
<i>Dad, I've done this many times.</i>

115
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:49,233
I agree, but it's still
dangerous.

116
00:04:49,367 --> 00:04:50,500
<i> Major...</i>

117
00:04:50,633 --> 00:04:51,700
You're right.

118
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:53,733
<i> But Joey is doing a good job.</i>

119
00:04:53,867 --> 00:04:56,867
She's sharp, resourceful,

120
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,433
and she knows how to fight.

121
00:04:58,567 --> 00:05:01,533
<i>But I promise you,
just like before,</i>

122
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:03,333
I won't let anything
happen to her.

123
00:05:03,467 --> 00:05:07,500
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

124
00:05:12,067 --> 00:05:14,567
[ROOSTER CROWING]

125
00:05:15,467 --> 00:05:17,800
Auntie Bebeng, that's your
fifth snack already.

126
00:05:17,933 --> 00:05:19,167
You'll finish all our snacks

127
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:21,033
if you keep eating like that.

128
00:05:21,367 --> 00:05:24,633
Why are you kids meddling
with everything, even my snacks.

129
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:27,600
Why don't you ask yourself

130
00:05:27,733 --> 00:05:29,033
if there's anything left
for you?

131
00:05:29,167 --> 00:05:31,167
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

132
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:33,067
You think I don't know

133
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:35,200
why you suddenly came home?

134
00:05:35,833 --> 00:05:37,900
You're probably running away
from someone...

135
00:05:38,033 --> 00:05:40,167
in Manila. Right?

136
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:44,567
But, Peter, how are you really?

137
00:05:46,633 --> 00:05:48,367
I'm okay, Auntie Beng.

138
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:51,667
I'll forget eventually.

139
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,367
That's not true.

140
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:54,967
You even dreamed about her.

141
00:05:55,367 --> 00:05:56,567
Wait.

142
00:05:56,700 --> 00:06:00,567
Does that mean if my crush
dreams about me,

143
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:01,933
she's in love with me too?

144
00:06:02,067 --> 00:06:04,133
There, that's where
you're good at.

145
00:06:04,267 --> 00:06:06,600
You, young people,

146
00:06:06,733 --> 00:06:09,067
have such shallow
perspective of love.

147
00:06:09,233 --> 00:06:11,200
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
When you're not chosen,

148
00:06:11,333 --> 00:06:14,000
that's it, it's the end
of the world for you.

149
00:06:14,133 --> 00:06:17,533
You change your looks,
you change yourself.

150
00:06:17,667 --> 00:06:18,767
That's not how life works.

151
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:20,000
Wow.

152
00:06:20,133 --> 00:06:23,333
Coming from you, Auntie Bebeng,
who's single for life?

153
00:06:23,467 --> 00:06:25,300
You, rascal!

154
00:06:25,433 --> 00:06:27,733
Hey, don't underestimate me.

155
00:06:27,867 --> 00:06:31,167
Before I decided
to be single forever,

156
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:34,433
I experienced all of that, okay?

157
00:06:34,567 --> 00:06:35,967
Been there, done that.

158
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:38,133
So don't disparage me

159
00:06:38,267 --> 00:06:39,933
with your love talk.

160
00:06:40,067 --> 00:06:44,033
- [SCOFFS]
- [PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

161
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,967
[KEYBOARD CLICKING]

162
00:06:57,833 --> 00:06:59,967
Is your keyboard working?

163
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:02,267
Of course, why?

164
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:05,233
So, you can keep the sound down.

165
00:07:05,367 --> 00:07:06,133
Sorry.
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

166
00:07:06,733 --> 00:07:08,233
Well, it's just that,
I just can't believe

167
00:07:08,367 --> 00:07:10,967
Major Delgado is still alive...

168
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:13,333
and still an undercover,
no less.

169
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:17,133
You really are father
and daughter...

170
00:07:18,133 --> 00:07:22,400
you're both certified
never-say-die.

171
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,767
The way you said it,
it's like we're bad people.

172
00:07:27,633 --> 00:07:29,300
And...

173
00:07:29,433 --> 00:07:31,967
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

174
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:35,000
It's really like that,
when you want something...

175
00:07:35,133 --> 00:07:37,533
you'll do everything to get it.

176
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:42,133
I'm sure it's not just me
and my dad who are like that.

177
00:07:42,267 --> 00:07:45,567
Hello? There are plenty
of people...

178
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:47,700
who can't move on.

179
00:07:47,867 --> 00:07:51,933
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

180
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:54,167
Wait, is this...

181
00:07:54,633 --> 00:07:56,167
about Zoey?

182
00:07:57,333 --> 00:07:58,500
Is this because...

183
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:02,033
she kissed me out of nowhere?

184
00:08:02,167 --> 00:08:05,633
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

185
00:08:06,433 --> 00:08:07,767
[PLINKS]

186
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:12,367
- [FIZZING]
- [UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

187
00:08:14,833 --> 00:08:16,300
<i> It dissolves fast, Madam.</i>

188
00:08:16,433 --> 00:08:19,133
<i>That means the stimulant's
purity is high.</i>

189
00:08:19,367 --> 00:08:20,400
<i> This is good, Madam.</i>

190
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:21,767
<i> Good.</i>

191
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:23,967
The kids will love this...

192
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:25,767
it hits fast.

193
00:08:28,233 --> 00:08:31,600
<i>I'm looking forward to our
shipment later.</i>

194
00:08:31,733 --> 00:08:34,100
<i>And I look forward
to the five hundred million.</i>

195
00:08:34,233 --> 00:08:36,267
[LAUGHS]

196
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:37,300
Oh, by the way,

197
00:08:37,433 --> 00:08:38,900
<i> as for transport,</i>

198
00:08:39,033 --> 00:08:40,667
<i> my man here, Francis,</i>

199
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:42,400
has already secured the route.

200
00:08:42,533 --> 00:08:43,533
And apparently...

201
00:08:44,233 --> 00:08:46,000
one of our brave policemen

202
00:08:46,133 --> 00:08:49,633
in Valmora is already
on our payroll.

203
00:08:49,767 --> 00:08:52,800
A pleasant surprise,
Captain Castro.

204
00:08:52,933 --> 00:08:53,967
Thank you, Madam!

205
00:08:54,633 --> 00:08:56,600
I'll take care of
my fellow officers.

206
00:08:56,733 --> 00:08:59,033
And as for those following
Berdugo,

207
00:08:59,167 --> 00:09:02,033
<i>we will neutralize them
before they get close.</i>

208
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,333
Following?

209
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:08,433
You mean you have active
threats?

210
00:09:11,133 --> 00:09:12,933
Just some small-time
competition.

211
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:15,033
Hardly worth my attention.
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

212
00:09:15,267 --> 00:09:17,600
<i>I've heard about you
for a long time, Berdugo.</i>

213
00:09:17,733 --> 00:09:20,433
And today, I'll finally meet you

214
00:09:21,067 --> 00:09:23,267
and see if you're actually
worth the fear

215
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,100
that follows your name.

216
00:09:25,233 --> 00:09:26,933
<i> But let me be clear...</i>

217
00:09:27,067 --> 00:09:30,000
if something goes wrong
with this deal,

218
00:09:30,167 --> 00:09:33,767
your Lumen-X will be history
in Valmora.

219
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:35,467
Don't forget, Delilah...

220
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,167
you're just a distributor.

221
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:39,233
I am the creator.

222
00:09:39,367 --> 00:09:40,767
<i> I have the labs,</i>

223
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:42,733
<i> while you only have your men.</i>

224
00:09:42,867 --> 00:09:45,833
While you do business
in your small province,

225
00:09:45,967 --> 00:09:47,900
I'm already conquering
the entire country.

226
00:09:48,533 --> 00:09:51,233
Don't get too comfortable

227
00:09:51,367 --> 00:09:53,167
<i> because I am not a gentleman.</i>

228
00:09:53,733 --> 00:09:55,933
I'm not the type to hold back
just because you're a woman.

229
00:09:56,067 --> 00:10:05,600
[DAUNTING MUSIC CONTINUES]

230
00:10:08,767 --> 00:10:11,000
<i>The chief is just waiting
for the medico legal's answer.</i>

231
00:10:11,133 --> 00:10:13,067
<i>They said they still need
to double-check.</i>

232
00:10:15,167 --> 00:10:16,700
Double-check?

233
00:10:16,833 --> 00:10:19,233
My husband's body has been
with them for so long.

234
00:10:19,367 --> 00:10:20,767
What else do they need?

235
00:10:20,900 --> 00:10:23,033
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

236
00:10:23,167 --> 00:10:26,500
Cruz, be honest with me.

237
00:10:27,333 --> 00:10:29,600
Will we still see Miguel's body?

238
00:10:30,467 --> 00:10:32,800
Will I still be able
to hold a wake for my husband?

239
00:10:32,933 --> 00:10:34,167
I'm sorry, Ma'am.

240
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,133
<i>There's just a process
we must follow.</i>

241
00:10:38,767 --> 00:10:40,400
We'll talk later.

242
00:10:41,567 --> 00:10:44,433
Ma'am, I'm sorry...

243
00:10:44,567 --> 00:10:47,067
I woke you up
because of my loud voice.

244
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:48,000
It's okay.

245
00:10:48,133 --> 00:10:50,433
But did I hear it right?

246
00:10:50,567 --> 00:10:53,600
You still can't hold a wake
for your husband?

247
00:10:53,733 --> 00:10:57,667
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

248
00:10:57,800 --> 00:10:58,633
That's what you think,

249
00:10:58,767 --> 00:11:01,267
but she's not the one
I'm talking about.

250
00:11:04,133 --> 00:11:06,633
Okay, fine. Let's say...

251
00:11:07,967 --> 00:11:09,333
it's her.

252
00:11:10,933 --> 00:11:13,000
Is it a red flag if...

253
00:11:14,167 --> 00:11:16,800
I get back together with her?
Is that desperate?

254
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,233
That's up to you.
It's your choice,

255
00:11:20,367 --> 00:11:21,867
whatever feels right for you.

256
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,133
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

257
00:11:23,267 --> 00:11:25,733
But do you want me to...

258
00:11:26,367 --> 00:11:28,067
feel that way about her?

259
00:11:29,367 --> 00:11:31,333
Why are you asking
so many questions?

260
00:11:31,933 --> 00:11:34,767
If that's what you want,
then go ahead.

261
00:11:35,633 --> 00:11:38,133
As for me, I've got different
priorities here in Valmora.

262
00:11:38,267 --> 00:11:40,033
Not your love life.

263
00:11:41,667 --> 00:11:43,267
Fine, chill.

264
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:47,067
But I hope...

265
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:52,000
I hope we accomplish
our mission,

266
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:55,800
so we can both go home

267
00:11:56,967 --> 00:12:00,000
without anyone bothering us
anymore.

268
00:12:00,133 --> 00:12:03,500
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

269
00:12:08,233 --> 00:12:12,433
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

270
00:12:14,767 --> 00:12:16,800
[DOOR CREAKS]

271
00:12:19,633 --> 00:12:20,933
Hey! Hey! Hey!

272
00:12:22,133 --> 00:12:23,033
Hey...

273
00:12:23,167 --> 00:12:24,200
[KNOCKS]

274
00:12:24,333 --> 00:12:25,633
Hey, we had an agreement,
remember?

275
00:12:25,767 --> 00:12:27,233
I always use the bathroom first!

276
00:12:27,367 --> 00:12:29,333
Come on, get out of there!

277
00:12:29,467 --> 00:12:32,067
<i> - You were taking too long!
-</i> You're so hard to deal with!

278
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:33,900
<i> Wait, I'll be quick.</i>

279
00:12:34,033 --> 00:12:34,967
<i> And you're lying down...</i>

280
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:36,533
<i> you're not even looking at me.</i>

281
00:12:36,667 --> 00:12:39,300
You always want to have it
your way.

282
00:12:39,433 --> 00:12:43,433
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

283
00:12:51,167 --> 00:12:52,333
Hey!

284
00:12:52,467 --> 00:12:54,067
Nice smile.

285
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,233
Are you talking to your crush?

286
00:12:55,367 --> 00:12:57,333
Yes, Peter,
I'm chatting with her now.

287
00:12:57,467 --> 00:12:59,467
Wow, you're leveling up.

288
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:00,433
She said she's just busy,

289
00:13:00,567 --> 00:13:02,167
that's why she hasn't replied.

290
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:04,000
She's got a lot going on
at school.

291
00:13:04,133 --> 00:13:06,433
She's in every org.

292
00:13:06,567 --> 00:13:08,033
That means she's active.

293
00:13:08,167 --> 00:13:09,333
That's amazing.

294
00:13:09,467 --> 00:13:11,433
That's why I like her.

295
00:13:11,567 --> 00:13:14,533
She's smart and responsible.
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

296
00:13:15,933 --> 00:13:17,500
Just like Joey...

297
00:13:17,633 --> 00:13:20,133
smart, responsible,

298
00:13:20,267 --> 00:13:21,900
loving to her family.

299
00:13:22,067 --> 00:13:23,633
Even though it's dangerous now,

300
00:13:23,767 --> 00:13:26,833
she takes the risk for them.

301
00:13:26,967 --> 00:13:29,233
It's hard to fall in love
with someone like that, Peter.

302
00:13:29,367 --> 00:13:31,167
You got lots of competition
for her attention.

303
00:13:32,567 --> 00:13:35,833
Peter, let me ask you...

304
00:13:35,967 --> 00:13:39,633
did Joey really tell you
she doesn't like you?

305
00:13:39,767 --> 00:13:43,567
No, but it feels that way.

306
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:44,700
Because she doesn't pay
attention

307
00:13:44,833 --> 00:13:47,233
to any of the interest
I'm showing her.

308
00:13:47,367 --> 00:13:48,800
Nothing.

309
00:13:48,933 --> 00:13:50,233
Are you sure?

310
00:13:50,367 --> 00:13:51,600
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

311
00:13:51,733 --> 00:13:53,467
Didn't you just say

312
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:57,267
she's facing great danger
for her family?

313
00:13:57,433 --> 00:14:02,300
Maybe she has bigger problems
to deal with,

314
00:14:02,433 --> 00:14:06,267
so she doesn't have time
for other things.

315
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:09,267
So, listen, both of you...

316
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:12,267
Always remember...

317
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:15,467
a person who truly loves,

318
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:19,300
never gets tired of waiting.

319
00:14:19,433 --> 00:14:21,633
Okay? Okay? Okay?

320
00:14:23,467 --> 00:14:26,833
Me, I've been waiting
for 48 years, still nothing.

321
00:14:26,967 --> 00:14:28,567
Life!

322
00:14:28,733 --> 00:14:31,167
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

323
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:34,000
<i>Hey, Keith, come here,
help me out!</i>

324
00:14:34,133 --> 00:14:35,200
All right!

325
00:14:38,767 --> 00:14:40,500
We need to add more people.

326
00:14:40,633 --> 00:14:42,833
Five hundred million
is at stake here.

327
00:14:42,967 --> 00:14:44,400
We can't afford to be
at a disadvantage.

328
00:14:44,533 --> 00:14:46,233
Francis...

329
00:14:48,367 --> 00:14:49,833
- Hi.
- Zoey.

330
00:14:49,967 --> 00:14:53,300
Are you busy? I was hoping
to invite you to dinner.

331
00:14:53,433 --> 00:14:55,267
I felt our last conversation
was cut short,

332
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:57,033
- you know.
- Oh, dinner?

333
00:14:57,167 --> 00:15:00,333
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]
Sorry, I can't.

334
00:15:02,633 --> 00:15:05,567
How about lunch?

335
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:08,033
- Lunch?
- Are you free for lunch?

336
00:15:08,167 --> 00:15:10,133
[CLICKS TONGUE]

337
00:15:10,267 --> 00:15:12,167
I've got a lot to do too,
I'm sorry, Zoey...

338
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:14,800
but Madam Delilah needs me.

339
00:15:14,933 --> 00:15:16,467
That's too bad.

340
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:19,500
You're always so busy.

341
00:15:19,633 --> 00:15:20,967
Sometimes I feel like
you're not really

342
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:22,867
the owner of this resort.

343
00:15:24,233 --> 00:15:25,733
Why do you say that?

344
00:15:26,633 --> 00:15:30,767
Because the resort owners
I know...

345
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:32,467
are chill.
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

346
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:34,900
But you, you handle
everything yourself.

347
00:15:36,433 --> 00:15:39,400
I'm just very hands-on, Zoey.

348
00:15:39,967 --> 00:15:42,333
But I have something
to tell you.

349
00:15:42,467 --> 00:15:44,267
Zoey, I'm interested in you.

350
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:47,267
I want to change.

351
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:50,333
Change?

352
00:15:56,600 --> 00:16:00,667
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

353
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:04,500
Wow, I'm glad you left
some for me.

354
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:07,200
Only one left?

355
00:16:07,333 --> 00:16:10,333
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

356
00:16:12,167 --> 00:16:13,533
Delicious.

357
00:16:18,033 --> 00:16:19,933
- What?
- Let me.

358
00:16:20,067 --> 00:16:22,100
See? You're not even listening
to anything.

359
00:16:22,233 --> 00:16:23,167
It was paused!

360
00:16:23,300 --> 00:16:24,600
You heard me,

361
00:16:24,733 --> 00:16:28,167
but you still took
the last<i> longganisa</i> .

362
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:29,233
Oh, come on.

363
00:16:29,367 --> 00:16:30,533
I was hungry.

364
00:16:31,633 --> 00:16:33,867
That was good for four...

365
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,600
you made it good for one.

366
00:16:35,733 --> 00:16:37,700
I said I was hungry!

367
00:16:39,167 --> 00:16:40,733
Wait, what's your problem?

368
00:16:43,767 --> 00:16:45,567
I'm hungry, that's all.

369
00:16:48,733 --> 00:16:50,467
Joey, is there
a problem between us?

370
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:52,300
What's your deal?

371
00:16:52,433 --> 00:16:53,700
I don't get you.

372
00:16:54,733 --> 00:16:57,733
My husband's death
was so sudden.

373
00:16:57,867 --> 00:16:59,400
And now, we don't even know

374
00:16:59,533 --> 00:17:02,033
if we can hold a wake
for Miguel.

375
00:17:04,333 --> 00:17:07,000
I'm sorry you're going
through this.

376
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:10,733
[SIGHS]

377
00:17:10,867 --> 00:17:13,967
How I wish I could
actually help you.

378
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:17,133
Back when I was...

379
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:21,200
the queen of headlines,
maybe I could.

380
00:17:22,067 --> 00:17:24,567
But now, here.

381
00:17:26,233 --> 00:17:28,567
I'm the queen of the headboard.

382
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:30,167
Bedridden royalty.

383
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:33,200
[CHUCKLES]
I'm sorry, Ma'am.

384
00:17:33,333 --> 00:17:34,167
I didn't...

385
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:35,967
I didn't mean to laugh.

386
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:38,500
It's okay, it's okay.

387
00:17:38,633 --> 00:17:40,533
I wanted you to laugh.

388
00:17:43,467 --> 00:17:47,000
Earlier, when I saw your anger,

389
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:50,367
your frustration, your grief...

390
00:17:51,467 --> 00:17:54,067
I knew it hurt more...

391
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,967
than my illness.

392
00:17:56,100 --> 00:17:58,267
Maybe that's how it is.

393
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:01,267
We all carry our own burdens.

394
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,933
Exactly.

395
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:06,400
So, what's your plan now?

396
00:18:09,633 --> 00:18:11,267
I don't know yet.

397
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:15,567
But Sir Tomas told me
he wants to help

398
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:18,700
with Miguel's drug case.

399
00:18:18,833 --> 00:18:21,167
Maybe I should talk
to Sir Tomas.

400
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:22,133
No!
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

401
00:18:22,967 --> 00:18:26,200
You don't need Tomas's help.

402
00:18:27,733 --> 00:18:29,700
Do not deal with him.

403
00:18:30,767 --> 00:18:32,833
And no matter what promises
he makes,

404
00:18:32,967 --> 00:18:36,867
no matter what help he says
he can give...

405
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,300
do not take it.

406
00:18:40,033 --> 00:18:42,100
Ma'am, why?

407
00:18:43,233 --> 00:18:45,800
What's going on with Sir Tomas?

408
00:18:45,933 --> 00:18:50,700
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

409
00:18:52,633 --> 00:18:54,267
Wow!

410
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:58,300
Our sweet patient is awake.

411
00:19:01,233 --> 00:19:03,867
You look startled.

412
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,567
Did something happen?
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

413
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:06,733
No, nothing.

414
00:19:06,867 --> 00:19:08,700
It's just that...

415
00:19:09,300 --> 00:19:12,633
Clarissa, she told me
a little ghost story.

416
00:19:12,767 --> 00:19:14,367
I was surprised by the ending.

417
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:16,833
I didn't expect it.

418
00:19:16,967 --> 00:19:19,567
Mom, stress is off limits.
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

419
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:21,967
The doctor was clear
about that, right?

420
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:23,167
Yes.

421
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:24,767
I'm fine, I'm fine.

422
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:27,300
Is it time for me
to take a bath?

423
00:19:27,433 --> 00:19:28,467
Oh, yes.

424
00:19:28,633 --> 00:19:30,033
Since Clarissa is new,

425
00:19:30,167 --> 00:19:32,333
I'll walk her through
the routine, okay?

426
00:19:32,467 --> 00:19:33,300
- Okay.
- Okay.

427
00:19:33,433 --> 00:19:35,433
Clarissa, let's do this.

428
00:19:35,567 --> 00:19:36,767
Okay, Mom.

429
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:38,600
- Yes.
- Okay, hold on.

430
00:19:38,733 --> 00:19:40,000
[GRUNTS]

431
00:19:41,067 --> 00:19:42,633
Slowly.

432
00:19:42,767 --> 00:19:45,100
There you go.

433
00:19:45,233 --> 00:19:46,767
Slippers.

434
00:19:46,900 --> 00:19:49,233
Here, here.

435
00:19:49,367 --> 00:19:50,667
Okay.

436
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:54,800
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

437
00:19:57,800 --> 00:19:59,567
I want to change.

438
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,300
Change?

439
00:20:02,467 --> 00:20:04,067
Change my life.

440
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:06,067
I want to have a family.

441
00:20:07,100 --> 00:20:09,400
I want to have children.

442
00:20:10,633 --> 00:20:12,400
But not here,
I want to be far away from here.

443
00:20:13,300 --> 00:20:15,500
That's why I need to finish
this last...

444
00:20:15,633 --> 00:20:17,133
Last what?
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

445
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:20,133
Investment.

446
00:20:20,267 --> 00:20:23,500
It's quite huge, and...

447
00:20:23,633 --> 00:20:25,133
the transaction
is scheduled for later.

448
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,033
But, Zoey, after that,

449
00:20:28,167 --> 00:20:30,867
I want a new life.

450
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:33,367
[LAUGHS]

451
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:35,467
Wow, you're moving too fast!
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

452
00:20:35,633 --> 00:20:37,567
We've only been on one date.

453
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:40,267
We just met.

454
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:42,167
Anyway...

455
00:20:42,300 --> 00:20:44,367
Have you spoken
to Madam Delilah?

456
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:47,733
Did you tell her
I want to work for her?

457
00:20:47,867 --> 00:20:49,433
About that?

458
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:52,033
Sure, I'll tell her.

459
00:20:53,267 --> 00:20:54,567
Thank you.

460
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:57,867
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

461
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:01,700
Joey, come on, let's go.

462
00:21:01,833 --> 00:21:03,267
Where?

463
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:05,267
Why are we here?

464
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:08,000
To look for evidence,

465
00:21:08,133 --> 00:21:09,700
information,

466
00:21:09,867 --> 00:21:11,533
for the mission.

467
00:21:11,667 --> 00:21:13,033
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

468
00:21:13,167 --> 00:21:16,167
Shouldn't Zoey
be with you for that?

469
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:18,600
I might just get in the way.

470
00:21:18,733 --> 00:21:20,267
You know, last night,

471
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:22,400
it was cute
that you were affected.

472
00:21:22,533 --> 00:21:24,633
But now...

473
00:21:24,767 --> 00:21:26,400
you're insecure.

474
00:21:27,567 --> 00:21:29,167
Excuse me!

475
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:30,867
Me, insecure?

476
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,900
Why would I be insecure?

477
00:21:33,033 --> 00:21:35,267
You can't move on from Zoey.

478
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:38,333
I don't need to move on...

479
00:21:38,467 --> 00:21:40,167
there's no issue for me.

480
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:41,667
You can marry her,

481
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:43,300
have kids with her.

482
00:21:43,467 --> 00:21:44,600
That's not an issue for me.

483
00:21:44,733 --> 00:21:46,433
I don't care.

484
00:21:46,567 --> 00:21:47,833
So, go ahead.

485
00:21:48,833 --> 00:21:50,667
Whatever, Joey.

486
00:21:50,800 --> 00:21:53,700
If you don't come with me,
I won't tell your father...

487
00:21:53,833 --> 00:21:55,967
if we get information.

488
00:21:56,100 --> 00:21:58,467
You're the only one
who can contact him.

489
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:02,567
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

490
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:14,067
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

491
00:22:18,233 --> 00:22:22,233
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

492
00:22:24,833 --> 00:22:27,367
When do I meet your business
partner, Berdugo?

493
00:22:27,500 --> 00:22:29,900
You do not meet him
whenever you want.

494
00:22:30,033 --> 00:22:32,767
I didn't agree to join here
just to be a nobody.

495
00:22:32,900 --> 00:22:35,267
But since it's official
and government sanctioned,

496
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:36,367
civilians are not allowed...

497
00:22:36,500 --> 00:22:39,133
I have it filed,
it's documented.

498
00:22:39,267 --> 00:22:40,500
You didn't.

499
00:22:40,633 --> 00:22:42,167
You're leaving,
and you'll leave me

500
00:22:42,300 --> 00:22:44,833
with some guy I haven't
even spoken to?

501
00:22:44,967 --> 00:22:47,333
My father needs to know
about the transaction.

502
00:22:47,467 --> 00:22:48,800
You know what I smell?

503
00:22:48,967 --> 00:22:50,567
The people looking for you.

504
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:52,367
Are they your problem?

505
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:53,400
We had an agreement.

506
00:22:53,533 --> 00:22:55,033
Honor that agreement.
